      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I super duper want this and am continually frustrated it's not a feature yet.\n- Someone on Discord recommends a World, I click the link, I say \"heck yeah!\" and then it goes down the memory hole, never to be seen again\n- THE WEBSITE ITSELF recommends me a \"totally random\" World, I say \"heck yeah!\" and never, ever visit it because ???? what was it called again",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-09T23:06:00.127Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Next to finding new friends, I love sightseeing in VRChat. Photogrammetrized worlds, art projects and the likes intrigue me to no end.\nTherefore, it would be really handy to be able to queue up worlds you want to visit via VRChat.com, then see the list in-game.\nExample: I find five worlds I like the looks of on VRChat.com, and instead of clicking \"Launch\" or \"Invite me\", I can click \"Add to queue\"\nThen, when I log in to VRChat, I will be able to click a button in my menu or the worlds page that shows me my queue. The game should automatically remove worlds from the queue as you visit them.\nAt the moment, the way I handle a queue of worlds I wanna visit is opening every world I wanna visit in tabs, and keeping them there until the next time I play VRChat. And I gotta say, it's not very ideal for a multitude of reasons :)\nCheck out my examples attached as images to this post.",
